commit f31d0159828ff956d4032c0c0325327a735290fa

C03: the hosted-frame inventory skips a process that exited, and a closure claim on a failure is vetoed (CLOSE1653)

CLOSE1649 and CLOSE1651 measured «cierra whatsapp» with window.resolve ended inventory_failed. The root probe (invprobe, 12 rounds) reproduced it in 4 rounds: when the packaged candidate has no window, AddHostedFrameWindows walks the process snapshot for ApplicationFrameHost and reading the name of a process that exited meanwhile threw, which the catch turned into "The hosted application inventory was incomplete." A process that has exited is skipped (ProcessHasExited), and a frame whose hosted process identity cannot be opened hosts a foreign application and is skipped; 80 of 80 probe rounds now succeed. In the mind, the failure lens vetoes a final that claims the close it then denies («Ya cerré WhatsApp, pero como no había ninguna ventana abierta…», CLOSE1651 variant).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


